{"kind":"report","text":"Checker review of the scope-index census recut, child f51f16f4, at exact head 52511ced8b6b5239272dae61911ccec18acfbea8, under builder promise d28d9bcd and ruling c0789349. Verdict: APPROVED.\n\n## What changed since ca32d20f\n\nThe recut descends from b5deace0 and merges landed Main c7b7d1b8. It changes 8 non-note paths, 115 lines added and 29 removed. These are the source changes:\n- `scopeIndexCensusRoute` now takes the trusted transport `address`, and `routedRequest` passes it.\n- After `requestOf` and the index check, the route runs the same edge `admitServing(env, { kind: \"signed-read\", reader }, address)` that the other signed reads use, before `owner.list`. It maps `invalid` to forbidden.\n- The owner's inner `rate` port and its call are removed, so the operator is charged once.\n\nThe owner's authorization chain is unchanged from what I approved in ca32d20f. The owner is reachable only through the fixed internal binding.\n\n## Witness\n\nA new Native test runs with key and address windows of 1 and counts the proof RPCs:\n- A non-operator key is first refused 403, after one proof RPC.\n- The same key from a new address is refused 429 with no proof RPC.\n- A new key from the same address is refused 429 with no proof RPC.\n- A fresh key and address reach authorization (403, second proof RPC).\n- The operator gets 200 with `next: null`. With limit 1, that would fail if the owner charged again.\n- The operator's second request is refused 429 with no proof RPC.\n\nThe note retains a control: moving admission back after the owner fails this witness on the proof count. The route rows in docs/security/entry-points.md now read \"address and key windows before the census owner\", and the inventory says no forwarded header supplies the address.\n\n## Evidence and gate\n\n- The gate ran at 9999fc38, tree e978f39b. gate/receipt.json records exit 0, source unchanged and no collection errors, and its output ends \"gate passed\".\n- After 9999fc38, only the note and the manifest change.\n- The manifest SHA-256 is fe90d213…, as stated.\n- All 70 files in 2026-10-27-scope-index-census-admission-repair match it, nothing is writable, and SHA256SUMS has 69 lines, all OK.\n\n## Conclusions\n\n- Architecture: approved, unchanged from ca32d20f. The authority chain, explicit paging end, bounds and publication of complete censuses only all match c0789349.\n- Security: approved. Every census request now passes the address and key windows before the fixed owner does any row or proof work, the same as the other signed reads. Operator authority is still the install signer of the pinned register.\n- Simplification: approved. The repair removes a port.\n\nStill owed by the planner after landing: deploying all three Workers, then the first census and version report on each. The landing check will follow the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ac88b93eff869e18911dbc914a7a8219e79f48a4","binding":"assigned","head":"52511ced8b6b5239272dae61911ccec18acfbea8","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:07739f55a9fcfcb89a35270c5a32a48c6a2281ed\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d28d9bcd02aa9374774c52e565f5b5c893c657f1\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:07739f55a9fcfcb89a35270c5a32a48c6a2281ed","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}